(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[12 1 "// The sys module (Python/sysmodule.c; PY5e): made once per interpreter on its first import (sysModule),"] [13 1 "// from the host's configuration (Configure: argv, the search path). sys.modules is the interpreter's"] [14 1 "// Modules, sys.stdout and sys.stderr write to its streams, sys.stdin reads the process's standard input."] [15 1 "// sys.implementation.name is \"arbace\" (PYS15 (a)): Lib/test's @cpython_only tests skip, as on PyPy."] [17 1 "// The host's configuration, set before a run (Configure)."] [23 1 "// Configure sets the next interpreters' sys.argv and sys.path (the script's directory first, then the"] [24 1 "// standard library's Lib), each list's items separated by NUL; bin/pyi's host calls it before RunModule"] [25 1 "// or Repl."] [47 1 "// sysVersion is sys.version: the language's version, then pyi's build in CPython's layout."] [50 1 "// pyVersion315 is the version under REPR_PYTHON_VERSION=3.15 (queue 252): the pin 3.15.2, its Lib on sys.path."] [58 1 "// textFile is a text stream of the process (sys.stdin, sys.stdout, sys.stderr): _io.TextIOWrapper's"] [59 1 "// interface over the interpreter's buffered streams. The rest of io is _pyio's (PY6)."] [63 19 "// what w buffers (writeErr)"] [66 2 "// enc, errs: reconfigure()'s encoding and errors, \"\" the process's (stdioConfig); lineBuf its line_buffering"] [67 2 "// (queue 286: inspect's command line reconfigures sys.stdout's errors)"] [70 2 "// writeThrough: every write flushed, write_through (py-mods-1122: create_stdio's !buffered_stdio, -u or"] [71 2 "// PYTHONUNBUFFERED; libregrtest's --fast-ci adds -u when sys.stdout.write_through is false; reconfigure sets it)"] [75 1 "// stdioUnbuffered is the start's buffered_stdio negated (pylifecycle.c's create_stdio): -u (bin/pyi python's"] [76 1 "// PYI_UNBUFFERED, read once and removed from the environment as PYI_IGNORE_ENV is) or PYTHONUNBUFFERED (not under -E or -I)"] [91 1 "// writeErr is a failed write's or flush's OSError (py-eval-1122: with SIGPIPE ignored a closed pipe is EPIPE, a"] [92 1 "// BrokenPipeError, as CPython's BufferedWriter raises it). bufio keeps a write error for every later write and flush, so"] [93 1 "// the buffered bytes are dropped and the writer starts again on what it buffers: json.tool's handler dup2s /dev/null over"] [94 1 "// stdout and exits with EPIPE's status, which the shutdown's flush (status 120 when it fails) leaves."] [105 1 "// encoding is the stream's encoding: reconfigure()'s, else the process's."] [113 1 "// errors is the stream's errors handler: reconfigure()'s, else the process's."] [127 1 "// processStdin is the process's standard input, buffered once for every interpreter."] [146 1 "// ioMethod is a built-in method of t (PY5c's AddMethod: the dictionary filled once str's hash is ready)."] [162 2 "// the standard streams' attributes (PY6b's request: doctest reads sys.stdout.encoding)"] [167 2 "// reconfigure (textio.c's _io_TextIOWrapper_reconfigure_impl; queue 286): encoding and errors (errors \"strict\" when"] [168 2 "// only the encoding is given), line_buffering (a line written flushes), write_through and newline checked; the"] [169 2 "// encoding looked up as the codec registry has it"] [285 4 "// a write error raises (queue 253: flush_std_files reports a failed flush at shutdown, status 120)"] [313 2 "// readlines(hint=-1) and iteration (py-design-1122: json.tool --json-lines reads sys.stdin.readlines()): IOBase's,"] [314 2 "// readline until the end, a positive hint stopping once the lines read hold that many characters"] [354 2 "// close (queue 249: multiprocessing's _close_stdin closes sys.stdin in a spawned child): the standard streams are"] [355 2 "// made with closefd=False (create_stdio), so the stream is flushed and marked closed, its descriptor left open"] [363 4 "// a failed flush raises after the close (TextIOWrapper.close: flush, then the buffer's close in a finally)"] [381 1 "// The standard streams' buffer (PY6e's REQUEST: subprocess's children write sys.stdout.buffer): a binary"] [382 1 "// view of the same bufio reader or writer, so text and bytes keep their order."] [473 3 "// iteration: the native BufferedReader's slots read the port's value, which a standard stream's buffer has"] [474 3 "// not (queue 545: its readline's lines)"] [498 1 "// exactArgsSelf checks a method's call: self and n arguments, no keywords."] [519 1 "// sysModule is the interpreter's sys module, made on first use."] [539 2 "// py-os-1124: bin/pyi python's PYI_ARGV, sys.argv's bytes as the command line gave them (\\x1f between them; read once"] [540 2 "// and removed from the environment), decoded as Py_DecodeLocale does under UTF-8 (surrogateescape): the host's"] [541 2 "// strings of configArgv lost an undecodable byte (test_cmd_line's test_invalid_utf8_arg)"] [553 31 "// a PYTHONPATH entry's undecodable bytes surrogate-escaped (py-os-1124)"] [566 2 "// the runtime's own text streams until the start replaces them (initSysStreams, queue 551): sys is made before"] [567 2 "// importlib stands, and a TextIOWrapper's codec lookup imports the encodings package"] [576 41 "// queue 553: create_stdio's None for a closed descriptor"] [585 15 "// 3.15 (queue 252, PY315-SURVEY P7): the version the standard library (3.15.2's Lib) moves with"] [592 25 "// types.SimpleNamespace (PY6b: FrozenImporter makes them)"] [594 45 "// pyi's own .pyc files (PY6b): __pycache__/NAME.arbace-314.pyc, its own magic number"] [600 2 "// sys.flags as python3 -s -P -B runs (the references'): the struct sequence of sysmodule.c's flags_desc"] [613 2 "// py-os-1124: -O, -v, -d, -B and their variables (config's optimization_level, verbose, parser_debug, write_bytecode),"] [614 2 "// and hash_randomization as config's use_hash_seed == 0 || hash_seed != 0 (PYTHONHASHSEED=0 without -R: 0)"] [626 47 "// -X int_max_str_digits, PYTHONINTMAXSTRDIGITS (py-eval-1122)"] [629 2 "// -q, -E and -I (queue 296): config's quiet, use_environment and isolated (-I also -E's)"] [639 2 "// -i (queue 289): inspect and interactive; PYTHONINSPECT at start: inspect"] [646 2 "// -X utf8[=0|1] and PYTHONUTF8 (py-mods-1122: 3.14's too, pyi's default 1 kept; test_io's test_text_encoding runs"] [647 2 "// children with -X utf8=0 and -X utf8=1); -X warn_default_encoding and PYTHONWARNDEFAULTENCODING (config's"] [648 2 "// warn_default_encoding, PEP 597: _pyio's text_encoding warns; test_io's test_check_encoding_warning)"] [658 3 "// 3.15's lazy imports (queue 239): sys.flags.lazy_imports, sys.lazy_modules and the mode's and filter's API"] [671 18 "// -X options (queue 220: bin/pyi python passes them in PYI_XOPTIONS)"] [680 2 "// the struct sequences of numbers and threads, with CPython 3.14's values (64-bit Linux)"] [693 2 "// sys.monitoring (PEP 669): its call-family events (queue 220, monitoring.go)"] [697 43 "// PY6c"] [700 2 "// pyi's own launcher when bin/pyi runs it (PY6e: tools/pyi/python3, CPython's command line), so that"] [701 2 "// script_helper and subprocess start pyi as CPython starts itself"] [707 2 "// config's pycache_prefix (py-os-1124, test_cmd_line's test_set_pycache_prefix): -X pycache_prefix=PATH, else"] [708 2 "// PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX (not under -E or -I); -X pycache_prefix with no or an empty PATH none"] [732 3 "// PyErr_SetObject(PyExc_SystemExit, status): a tuple's items are the exception's arguments, None none"] [788 5 "// PyErr_GetExcInfo: the type, the exception, its __traceback__ (queue 223)"] [817 40 "// -1: -X cpu_count unset (os.process_cpu_count from sched_getaffinity)"] [858 53 "// sys__getframe_impl's audit (queue 536)"] [864 2 "// breakpointhook (queue 304): sys_breakpointhook, $PYTHONBREAKPOINT's callable (pdb.set_trace when unset or empty, a"] [865 2 "// no-op for \"0\", a name without a dot builtins'), an unimportable one warned of and ignored; -E and -I ignore the"] [866 2 "// environment (Py_GETENV)"] [890 3 "// PyImport_Import: the leaf module (a non-empty fromlist)"] [908 2 "// the hooks and introspection the stdlib reads at import (PY6a: threading, test.support)"] [914 4 "// _PyErr_Display: the traceback given put on an exception that has none (issue #18776)"] [922 4 "// traceback's display raises for a non-exception; the C fallback's print_exception line (queue 223)"] [931 2 "// is_remote_debug_enabled (queue 223): False, as a CPython built without Py_REMOTE_DEBUG answers (pyi has no"] [932 2 "// remote debugging, :remote-debugging); test_sys imports it at its top"] [993 3 "// dataclasses' slots=True (gh-135228): __dict__ and __weakref__ taken out of a heap type's dict"] [1011 2 "// get_asyncgen_hooks and set_asyncgen_hooks (sysmodule.c; asyncio's event loops set theirs around run_forever):"] [1012 2 "// the running thread's hooks, a sys.asyncgen_hooks; an argument left out keeps its hook, None clears it"] [1046 2 "// _PySys_SetIntMaxStrDigits: 0 (no limit) or at least 640, sys.flags.int_max_str_digits with it (queue 202: a no-op,"] [1047 2 "// so test_decimal's PyCoverage, which sets 7000, met the 4300 digits' limit)"] [1070 2 "// sys.getprofile and sys.setprofile: the legacy profiler over sys.monitoring (queue 220, monitoring.go)"] [1077 2 "// sys.gettrace and sys.settrace: the legacy tracer over sys.monitoring (queue 219t, trace.go)"] [1104 2 "// threading.settrace_all_threads and setprofile_all_threads: every thread's trace or profile function"] [1147 24 "// its functions' __module__ \"sys\" (PY6f's REQUEST 8, as importBuiltin tags the others)"] [1151 1 "// displayHook is sys.displayhook: None prints nothing; another value's repr is written to sys.stdout and"] [1152 1 "// bound to builtins._ (the REPL's expression statements)."] [1181 1 "// displayUnencodable is sys_displayhook_unencodable (py-os-1124, test_cmd_line's test_displayhook_unencodable): a repr"] [1182 1 "// the stream's encoding cannot encode written encoded with backslashreplace, to the stream's buffer when it has one,"] [1183 1 "// else decoded again and written as text."] [1230 1 "// sysAttr is sys.NAME when the sys module exists and has it, else nil."] [1238 1 "// sysModuleIfAny is the interpreter's sys module once made (interp->sysdict: sys.modules' entry is not needed, queue"] [1239 1 "// 253), else the one in sys.modules, else nil."] [1250 1 "// initSysStreams is pylifecycle.c's init_sys_streams (queue 551, 545-1 (b), the user's decision of 2026-11-23): at"] [1251 1 "// the start, once the import system can import the encodings package, sys.stdin, sys.stdout and sys.stderr (and their"] [1252 1 "// __std*__) become create_stdio's TextIOWrapper(Buffered*(FileIO(fd))) when the interpreter writes to the process's"] [1253 1 "// descriptors; a stream that cannot be made (a closed descriptor) keeps the runtime's textFile, as an interpreter"] [1254 1 "// that writes elsewhere keeps all three."] [1287 1 "// createStdio is pylifecycle.c's create_stdio: _io.open(fd, \"wb\" or \"rb\", buffering, closefd=False), its raw stream"] [1288 1 "// named NAME, under a TextIOWrapper with the process's encoding and errors (stdioConfig), newline \"\\n\", line buffering"] [1289 1 "// for a terminal and for stderr, write_through under -u (no buffer: the raw stream itself), mode \"w\" or \"r\"; nil when"] [1290 1 "// a step fails (the caller keeps its textFile) or when the descriptor is not open (CPython's is_valid_fd: None then,"] [1291 1 "// left to the textFile here)."] [1335 1 "// flushStdObjects is flush_io: sys.stderr's and sys.stdout's flush, errors ignored (the REPL's prompt, input())."] [1352 1 "// writeTo writes s to a file object: the interpreter's stdout when f is nil or None, a textFile directly,"] [1353 1 "// else f.write(s)."] [1373 1 "// exactArgsN checks a function's call: n positional arguments, no keywords (CPython's messages)."] [1387 1 "// cpythonSizeof is sys.getsizeof as CPython 3.14 answers it on a 64-bit build for the core immutable types"] [1388 1 "// and the list and tuple (the list's allocation taken as its length), 0 for any other object (PY6b's"] [1389 1 "// request: test_marshal sizes its big-memory tests by sys.getsizeof of an int at import). py-mods-1122: also a"] [1390 1 "// dict (dictSizeof), and in getsizeof a weak reference or proxy and a heap type's instance (objectSizeof:"] [1391 1 "// object.__sizeof__'s tp_basicsize, 16 and 8 a slot, with getsizeof's pre-header, the GC header and the managed"] [1392 1 "// __dict__ and __weakref__ pointers), so the pure OrderedDict's __sizeof__ (its __dict__, its map, its links and"] [1393 1 "// proxies) answers."] [1399 30 "// OrderedDict.__sizeof__ and the GC header"] [1413 36 "// sizeof(PyByteArrayObject) + ob_alloc"] [1438 1 "// objectSizeof is getsizeof's answer for a weak reference or proxy and a heap type's instance (sys.getsizeof's alone:"] [1439 1 "// tracemalloc's sizes are cpythonSizeof's), 0 for any other object."] [1443 18 "// sizeof(PyWeakReference), the GC header"] [1448 35 "// the built-in base's size (0: unknown here)"] [1453 12 "// Py_TPFLAGS_PREHEADER: the managed __dict__ and __weakref__ pointers"] [1455 17 "// the GC header (a heap type with a __dict__, a __weakref__ or slots is collected)"] [1460 1 "// dictSizeof is _PyDict_SizeOf with getsizeof's GC header: sizeof(PyDictObject) 48, the GC header 16, and a"] [1461 1 "// non-empty dict's keys object (PyDictKeysObject's 32 bytes, a byte of index a slot up to 256 slots, the usable"] [1462 1 "// two thirds of its slots as entries, 16 bytes each when every key is a str, else 24), its size the smallest power"] [1463 1 "// of two from 8 whose usable part holds the dict's entries."] [1493 1 "// versionInfoType is sys.version_info's struct sequence (PY6b's request: test_importlib reads its releaselevel):"] [1494 1 "// a tuple with the fields' names."] [1531 1 "// asyncgenHooks are each thread's async generator hooks (firstiter, finalizer; nil unset, None too), as the thread"] [1532 1 "// state's async_gen_firstiter and async_gen_finalizer: firstiter called on an async generator's first __anext__, asend,"] [1533 1 "// athrow or aclose (coro.go's asyncGenInitHooks; asyncio's tracking of unfinished async generators for"] [1534 1 "// shutdown_asyncgens); the finalizer kept, never called (pyi has no finalization, PY7)."] [1539 1 "// stdlibAdded315 and stdlibRemoved315 are 3.15.2's Python/stdlib_module_names.h against 3.14.10's (queue 252): its"] [1540 1 "// 296 names."] [1545 1 "// stdlibModuleNames is sys.stdlib_module_names (Python/stdlib_module_names.h of CPython 3.14.10, its 297 names; queue 223:"] [1546 1 "// traceback's \"Did you forget to import\" reads it)"] [1582 1 "// utf8Mode315 is 3.15's UTF-8 mode (PEP 686, Python/initconfig.c's config_init_utf8_mode; queue 237): on by default,"] [1583 1 "// -X utf8=0 (or PYTHONUTF8=0, which -E and -I ignore) turns it off, -X utf8 and -X utf8=1 on. 3.14's answer stays"] [1584 1 "// pyi's 1 (the locale's coercion pyi does not model)."] [1598 1 "// utf8Mode314 is 3.14's UTF-8 mode (PEP 540, Python/preconfig.c's preconfig_init_utf8_mode; queue 553): -X utf8[=0|1],"] [1599 1 "// else PYTHONUTF8 (0 or 1; -E and -I ignore it), else on only when LC_CTYPE's locale (LC_ALL, LC_CTYPE, LANG, musl's"] [1600 1 "// default C.UTF-8) is the C or POSIX locale. Under C.UTF-8 the standard streams' errors stay surrogateescape (a locale"] [1601 1 "// coercion target's, config_get_stdio_errors), so only open()'s and TextIOWrapper's default encoding (the locale's) and"] [1602 1 "// sys.flags change."] [1622 1 "// utf8ModeCheck315 is preconfig_init_utf8_mode's refusals (3.15; queue 237; 3.14's too since queue 553): -X utf8=V and PYTHONUTF8 other than 0 or 1"] [1623 1 "// are a fatal error at start, status 1"] [1641 2 "// 3.14's preconfig_init_utf8_mode refuses the same values (queue 553)"] [1645 1 "// startWarnOptions is sys.warnoptions as config_init_warnoptions orders it (queue 328), the lowest precedence first:"] [1646 1 "// \"default\" in development mode, PYTHONWARNINGS's comma-separated options (not under -E